<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bhaktapur</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bhadgaon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bhaktapur is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu-valley">Kathmandu Valley</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>, about 13 km east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu">Kathmandu</a>. It was the capital of the Malla kings of the whole valley until the late 15th century and then of the independent Kingdom of Bhaktapur until the Gorkha conquest of 1769. Its Durbar Square, palace and temples, such as the five-storey Nyatapola, are part of the Kathmandu Valley World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bhaktapur.jpg" alt="Bhaktapur" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Saroj Pandey · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nyatpola_%26_Bhairav_Temple.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
